      "is_best": true,
      "html": "<div class=\"reply__content post__content post__content--new-editor\"><p>Well, that’s the range of sensors which ST has.</p><p>If you don’t see anything there suitable for your (unstated) application requirements, then you’ll obviously have to look elsewhere.</p><p> </p><p>But, as ​<user-mention data-id=\"8205\">@TDK</user-mention> said, we live in a 3D world - so any real gyro can only have 3 axes</p><p> </p><p><strong><u>PS</u>:</strong></p><p>You can combine an LSM6DSOX + LIS3MDL to give you 9 DOF; eg,</p><p><a href=\"https://www.adafruit.com/product/4517\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow ugc\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.adafruit.com/product/4517</a></p><p> </p><p>Other sensors, of course, can be used: <a href=\"https://embeddedcomputing.com/technology/analog-and-power/basics-of-6dof-and-9dof-sensor-fusion\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener nofollow ugc\" target=\"_blank\">Basics of 6DOF and 9DOF sensor fusion</a></p><p> </p><p>PPS:</p><p>See also:</p><oembed url=\"https://community.st.com/mems-sensors-48/9-axis-sensor-fusion-implementation-dt0058-dt0060-161638\"></oembed><p>which refers to:</p><p>Design tip <a href=\"https://www.st.com/resource/en/design_tip/dt0058-computing-tilt-measurement-and-tiltcompensated-ecompass-stmicroelectronics.pdf\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener nofollow ugc\" target=\"_blank\"><strong>DT0058</strong></a>, <em>Computing tilt measurement and tilt-compensated eCompass</em></p><p>Design tip <a href=\"https://www.st.com/resource/en/design_tip/dt0060-exploiting-the-gyroscope-to-update-tilt-measurement-and-ecompass-stmicroelectronics.pdf\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener nofollow ugc\" target=\"_blank\"><strong>DT0060</strong></a>, <em>Exploiting the gyroscope to update tilt measurement and eCompass</em></p></div>"
    },
    {
      "is_best": false,
      "html": "<div class=\"post__content post__content--new-editor\"><p>You can find ST’s full range of gyroscopes here: </p><p><a href=\"https://www.st.com/en/mems-and-sensors/gyroscopes/products.html\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow ugc\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.st.com/en/mems-and-sensors/gyroscopes/products.html</a></p><p>See also: <a href=\"https://www.st.com/en/mems-and-sensors/gyroscopes.html\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow ugc\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.st.com/en/mems-and-sensors/gyroscopes.html</a></p></div>"
    },
    {
      "is_best": false,
      "html": "<div class=\"post__content post__content--new-editor\"><p>It's 3 axis gyroscope u have send , i wanna know if 6 or 9 axis gyroscope mems exit for phones </p></div>"
    },
    {
      "is_best": false,
      "html": "<div class=\"post__content post__content--new-editor\"><p>As the space we mortals inhabit is three dimensional, you will only see up to 3-axis gyroscopes here on Earth. Perhaps you are confusing this with a 9-DOF sensor.</p></div>"
    }
  ]
